cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite both the accompanying paper and the
  FedBCa dataset it was evaluated on.
title: >-
  Federated Multi-Task Learning for Bladder Tumor Segmentation and MIBC
  Classification Using a Hybrid CNN-Transformer Architecture
abstract: >-
  Research code for a federated multi-task learning framework that jointly
  performs bladder tumor segmentation and MIBC/NMIBC classification from
  T2-weighted MRI across four clinical centers. The proposed Swin Hybrid model
  combines a ResNet-34 CNN branch with a Swin-Tiny Transformer branch and a
  segmentation-guided classification mechanism, trained with FedAvg.
type: software
license: MIT
keywords:
  - federated learning
  - multi-task learning
  - medical image segmentation
  - bladder cancer
  - MIBC classification
  - vision transformer
